* text=auto eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# CAPTURED PTY LOGS ARE BINARY, whatever their extension says.
#
# These are real terminal byte streams kept as test fixtures: escape sequences, bare CRs used for
# cursor returns, and CRLF pairs that are part of what the terminal actually emitted. `text=auto`
# would rewrite every CR out of the blob, so the fixture checked out on Linux would not be the bytes
# that were captured -- and a test asserting on a REAL capture would then be asserting on an edited
# one, silently, on one platform only. Added 2026-08-26 when two such fixtures were committed and git
# warned it was about to normalise them.
service/tests/data/console_keyboard_protocol_capture.txt -text
mcp/stdio/tests/fixtures/claude-generating-console-tail.txt -text
